#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105534 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105930 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "305f1d10-f98a-5849-a566-549265b3508d" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Square From a Diagram"}] :question/id #uuid "f7dc8ebd-817d-5709-99a5-f21dc726c2d0" :question/math-academy-id "e-2936" :question/problem "What is the area of the square shown below?\n\n![](images/53/53ab7a043ebbe03245fd0f8e1bf6438897a30d91654b6e51194205e4c302c07f.png)" :question/worked-solution "The area of a square with sides of length $a$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\mathcal{A} = a^2.\n$$\n\nNote that each side of a grid cell measures $3\\,\\textrm{ft},$ and each side of the shaded square covers $4$ grid cells. So, the length of each side of the shaded square is\n\n$$\na = 3 \\times 4 = 12 \\, \\textrm{ft} .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the shaded square is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={a}^{2}={12}^{2}=144\\,{ft}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105537 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105932 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b8e574a9-a37d-512f-aa4d-543ad1a3de84" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Rectangle From a Diagram"}] :question/id #uuid "cf89adb1-3344-5ed4-b2e0-48506af917bc" :question/math-academy-id "e-2940" :question/problem "A cinema has a rectangular hall whose dimensions are shown in the figure below. What is the area of the hall?\n\n![](images/e7/e7263eb3d75ecb243301c2d6c5712dd77232b97b6839123febec3260b389b2e6.png)" :question/worked-solution "The area of a rectangle is given by \n\n$$\n\\mathcal{A} = a \\cdot b,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are the lengths of the sides.\n\nFrom the figure, we obtain that \n\n$$\na = 4.5\\,\\mathrm{m}, \\qquad b = 6\\,\\mathrm{m}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the area of the hall is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =a\\cdot b=4.5\\cdot 6=27\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105538 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105935 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0726a51-b1a9-5755-a19b-0cc68f96b875" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Length of a Side of a Rectangle Given Another Side and Its Area"}] :question/id #uuid "022da369-7dfd-5865-8e72-4317203ad11e" :question/math-academy-id "e-2941" :question/problem "The area of the rectangular field shown below is $2\\,400\\,\\textrm{m}^2.$ What is the value of $x?$\n\n![](images/94/9419ae4a3099216109bff99906e5d1724a8f01f61e48e22edc62c0e1b62a1bef.png)" :question/worked-solution "The area of a rectangle is given by \n\n$$\n\\mathcal{A} = a \\cdot b,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are the lengths of the sides.\n\nFrom the figure, we obtain that \n\n$$\n\\mathcal{A} = 2\\,400\\mathrm{m}^2, \\qquad a = 60\\,\\mathrm{m}, \\qquad b=x .\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =a\\cdot b \\\\ 2\\,400 & =60\\cdot x \\\\ x & =\\frac{2\\,400}{60} \\\\ x & =40\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105671 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105838 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "85c79564-93e7-5054-9534-71dc8dc54f7b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Rectangle or a Square Given Its Perimeter"}] :question/id #uuid "08cf33de-c71e-55bb-8906-112075c06a37" :question/math-academy-id "e-7691" :question/problem "Find the area of the rectangle $ABCD$ if its perimeter is $40$ and ${BC} = 12.$" :question/worked-solution "We can find the length of ${AB}$ by using the formula for the perimeter, as follows:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =AB+BC+CD+DA \\\\ p & =2AB+2BC \\\\ 40 & =2AB+2(12) \\\\ 40 & =2AB+24 \\\\ 2AB & =16 \\\\ AB & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the rectangle $ABCD$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =AB\\cdot BC \\\\  & =8\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =96.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508962 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105838 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "85c79564-93e7-5054-9534-71dc8dc54f7b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Rectangle or a Square Given Its Perimeter"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "147d44b6-be70-5985-87d2-359212c64abf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "70" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508421} {:answer/id #uuid "4ba6dc5d-2df7-5ff1-9d5c-1e987f6e3b36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "92" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508501} {:answer/id #uuid "86e179f4-f4b1-5e05-a5f4-196353e934d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "85" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508589} {:answer/id #uuid "cbe3798c-bab3-5379-b806-51f51ae37774" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508713} {:answer/id #uuid "e12b6b48-1bc0-5cef-872e-4ec7e81b37b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508746}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cbe3798c-bab3-5379-b806-51f51ae37774" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508713} :answer-field/id #uuid "e48cd3c9-0b59-5bac-b974-bed484653ace" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508895}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9fa4030e-f9e5-59f6-ba9d-65a980d49dfe" :question/math-academy-id "q-117071" :question/problem "Find the area of the rectangle $ABCD$ if its perimeter is $36$ and $BC=10.$" :question/worked-solution "We can find the length of $AB$ by using the formula for the perimeter, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =AB+BC+CD+DA \\\\ p & =2AB+2BC \\\\ 36 & =2AB+2(10) \\\\ 36 & =2AB+20 \\\\ 2AB & =16 \\\\ AB & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the rectangle $ABCD$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =AB\\cdot BC \\\\  & =10\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =80.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508961 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105930 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "305f1d10-f98a-5849-a566-549265b3508d" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Square From a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03de657b-46bc-5dde-8c43-330d74e9b648" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508393} {:answer/id #uuid "1456890e-75d0-549d-8079-a328093ce956" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508420} {:answer/id #uuid "1a60e3b4-8113-5635-b39f-7eaebb4ff363" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508432} {:answer/id #uuid "8c72d778-672c-59f3-8acb-ac99286d54b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508601} {:answer/id #uuid "dd31e868-7aca-569d-85dd-2555e24bdd5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508742}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a60e3b4-8113-5635-b39f-7eaebb4ff363" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508432} :answer-field/id #uuid "f89de56d-ac6c-534d-88b4-b655b72b78ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508907}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9d8646f3-f09f-5c98-8c8f-8b6c0f35dfe5" :question/math-academy-id "q-117179" :question/problem "![](images/e0/e0a9d0aeba77f3ca2cd472b9c65df156394990a89a643e9a316ee662a52eb6b3.png)\n\nDavid wants to redesign his house, changing a small window for a big square window. The dimensions of the square window are shown in the figure above. What area covers the window?" :question/worked-solution "The area of a square with sides of length $a$ is given by \n\n$$\nA={a}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFrom the figure, we obtain that $a=4\\,m.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={a}^{2}={4}^{2}=16\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508971 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105930 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "305f1d10-f98a-5849-a566-549265b3508d" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Square From a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c720ea8-dccc-543a-aeb3-89a2e236ca67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "49\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508477} {:answer/id #uuid "4115a1b9-36b7-524d-9e1b-d151a5cbc361" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508484} {:answer/id #uuid "578b0918-88d0-55e9-8da6-226d9d8b7b75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508519} {:answer/id #uuid "7b17b055-bee6-5e61-a432-b94d1d81ecdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508571} {:answer/id #uuid "c66c5919-00de-52e0-8e67-17e321393e5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508698}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c720ea8-dccc-543a-aeb3-89a2e236ca67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "49\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508477} :answer-field/id #uuid "efc75398-cc75-59e2-8528-2b244f9d9f26" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508901}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bbbaba03-02d6-5c29-9b46-9da0f0be8cbb" :question/math-academy-id "q-117181" :question/problem "![](images/c3/c3f298b4df4e0c8ff66ad9da970c16ab11839f014519fd451dfba050500d9513.png)\n\nA family is having a picnic in a park. They place a big square blanket on the ground. The dimensions of the blanket are shown in the figure above. What is the area covered by the blanket?" :question/worked-solution "The area of a square with sides of length $a$ is given by \n\n$$\nA={a}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFrom the figure, we obtain that $a=7\\,ft.$ \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={a}^{2}={7}^{2}=49\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508966 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105932 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b8e574a9-a37d-512f-aa4d-543ad1a3de84" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Rectangle From a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41151962-0dd9-572c-96e9-fc4feef8073d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11\\,000\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508483} {:answer/id #uuid "4b9b7239-8ac1-5cee-bf69-99f6fbd3fc48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13\\,000\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508500} {:answer/id #uuid "664ce2e7-5431-5dd8-bd05-3a8b7d8e846d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\,000\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508542} {:answer/id #uuid "75e6271a-2f89-50d8-93ce-5d808e712bbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,000\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508559} {:answer/id #uuid "bb4ec6fa-3905-5dc7-ac24-fccd33798378" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\,000\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508672}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75e6271a-2f89-50d8-93ce-5d808e712bbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,000\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508559} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e4da27b-2dce-5bd1-a672-f45817b5055e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508841}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a60833b6-ee33-5277-9b1d-5d1fccd3856a" :question/math-academy-id "q-117186" :question/problem "![](images/eb/ebb60aa69c324ef1bfc70bc325ff71eca70426225859350c4bbd8a58a82a2757.png)\n\nThe parking lot in a market has a rectangular form whose dimensions are shown in the figure above. What is the area of the parking lot?" :question/worked-solution "The area of a rectangle is given by \n\n$$\nA=a\\cdot b,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are the lengths of the sides.\n\nFrom the figure, we obtain that \n\n$$\na=200\\,m,\\,b=60\\,m.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,  the area of the field is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =a\\cdot b=200\\cdot 60=12\\,000\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508923 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105838 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "85c79564-93e7-5054-9534-71dc8dc54f7b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Rectangle or a Square Given Its Perimeter"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "538c3464-d6d4-5422-a36d-0a0043f95251" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508512}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "538c3464-d6d4-5422-a36d-0a0043f95251" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508512} :answer-field/id #uuid "7cdfb13a-f513-5cd8-ae5d-a5e74bfaf7ee" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508850}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "404f0ec1-ce52-56bd-b28f-4f5a47723b39" :question/math-academy-id "q-171945" :question/problem "The perimeter of the rectangle $ABCD$ is $32.$ If $AB=3BC,$ then its area is $A=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Let $BC=x.$\n\nSince the perimeter of the rectangle is $p=32$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =AB+BC+CD+DA \\\\ p & =2(AB)+2(BC) \\\\ 32 & =2(3x)+2(x) \\\\ 32 & =6x+2x \\\\ 8x & =32 \\\\ x & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain $BC=4$ and $AB=3\\cdot 4=12.$\n\nTherefore, the area of a rectangle $ABCD$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =AB\\cdot BC \\\\  & =12\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =48.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508986 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105932 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b8e574a9-a37d-512f-aa4d-543ad1a3de84" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Rectangle From a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4680e928-ba75-5e32-b8a7-6fc72e31205d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508496} {:answer/id #uuid "aadcf2f2-5ca0-5416-90d4-f9a76cd9413a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508649} {:answer/id #uuid "c1e70cc4-b54b-5060-9470-1102d68bc62d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508688} {:answer/id #uuid "e1c4ff5e-1dad-5365-9d58-80e9b4d5e154" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "81\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508747} {:answer/id #uuid "f5b5c4b1-092b-5ffc-b03e-7f00c447bda0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508793}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1e70cc4-b54b-5060-9470-1102d68bc62d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508688} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc90adbc-d567-5552-83aa-263b9e6bc19f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508910}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "da7691ce-ed2d-5165-8a4d-fdf1f9bd503b" :question/math-academy-id "q-53230" :question/problem "![](images/47/473b8a18bb4d2bf77cfe18eb735bcb64ec95a551faadb18ad38f561c81d3b99c.png)\n\nFind the area of the rectangle $ABCD$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "The area of a rectangle is given by \n\n$$\nA=a\\cdot b,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are the lengths of the sides.\n\nFrom the figure, we obtain that \n\n$$\na=AB=9\\,cm,\\,b=AD=5\\,cm.\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, the area of the rectangle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =a\\cdot b=9\\cdot 5=45\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106416 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105935 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0726a51-b1a9-5755-a19b-0cc68f96b875" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Length of a Side of a Rectangle Given Another Side and Its Area"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f0416e4-9fea-506b-aeca-f53c05795336" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15\\,{\\text{yd}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508410} {:answer/id #uuid "8752afd1-f7b3-5a00-a5f6-d480894af162" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "500\\,\\text{yd}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508591} {:answer/id #uuid "985d6f45-92ac-5d55-8b62-94279162d932" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25\\,\\text{yd}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508619} {:answer/id #uuid "ea757878-f4e8-5eaf-8d63-8a16527b1941" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20\\,\\text{yd}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508764} {:answer/id #uuid "f4f5e77b-84f1-5eb3-b451-184e0ab46010" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30\\,\\text{yd}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508790}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "985d6f45-92ac-5d55-8b62-94279162d932" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25\\,\\text{yd}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508619} :answer-field/id #uuid "2dfd1944-ce2e-5b28-a2cd-855b60691175" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104644}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b96e524d-8067-5f5c-9997-cc35f0bb446f" :question/math-academy-id "q-53269" :question/problem "![](images/91/91a554b467201b7507b531dcc0b6e1d5d9970d3e6d6554878644a31e5e38d9fa.png)\n\nThe area of the rectangular field shown above is $500\\,{\\text{yd}}^{2}.$ What is the value of $x?$" :question/worked-solution "The area of a rectangle is given by \n\n$$\nA=a\\cdot b,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are the lengths of the sides.\n\nFrom the figure, we obtain that \n\n$$\na=20\\,yd,\\,A=500\\,{yd}^{2},\\,b=x.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =a\\cdot b \\\\ 500 & =20\\cdot x \\\\ x & =\\frac{500}{20} \\\\ x & =25\\,\\text{yd}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508939 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105935 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0726a51-b1a9-5755-a19b-0cc68f96b875" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Length of a Side of a Rectangle Given Another Side and Its Area"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d1b9500-8c1e-52f2-af98-5cf3b4505950" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,yd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508407} {:answer/id #uuid "415830b2-4096-54b1-a1e0-46e1dfd68021" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,yd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508486} {:answer/id #uuid "b5823cf8-062c-5722-8501-a426a438dd0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,yd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508661} {:answer/id #uuid "b69cffb8-30df-591a-bace-f9c4e3d14f00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\,yd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508664} {:answer/id #uuid "f47bdc75-a728-5b31-bfab-d252c6171250" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\,yd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508787}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b69cffb8-30df-591a-bace-f9c4e3d14f00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\,yd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508664} :answer-field/id #uuid "a85c8dd0-4a9d-5964-a329-cd025d7bcde3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508868}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6c1d9607-760c-5f72-b720-f7fb112fffe1" :question/math-academy-id "q-53279" :question/problem "![](images/54/547debca3e0215ebad8db2c525f9d1b0d435379c081073013cdbfd52b1b6c0f9.png)\n\nThe area of the rectangular court shown above is $56\\,{\\text{yd}}^{2}.$ What is the value of $x?$" :question/worked-solution "The area of a rectangle is given by \n\n$$\nA=a\\cdot b,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are the lengths of the sides.\n\nFrom the figure, we obtain that \n\n$$\na=2x-6\\,yd,\\,A=56\\,{yd}^{2},\\,b=7\\,\\text{yd}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =a\\cdot b \\\\ 56 & =(2x-6)\\cdot 7 \\\\ 56 & =14x-42 \\\\ 98 & =14x \\\\ x & =7\\,yd.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
